{"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/matomoencoding\/matomobatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MatomoBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and its limits:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let matomo = try HTTPDestination.matomo(","    url: url,  \/\/ where Matomo is installed: https:\/\/analytics.example.com","    siteID: 3,  \/\/ the app's site in Matomo","    dimensions: [\"plan\": 1, \"seats\": 2],  \/\/ custom dimensions made in Matomo","    category: \"Shop\",  \/\/ each event's category","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"requests\":[…]}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"requests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are one tracking request per record, oldest first, as Matomo asks for them: each a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string, ","type":"text"},{"code":"?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the request’s query, every value percent-encoded but for RFC 3986’s unreserved","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters. Each request is a Matomo event, with these parameters in this order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameter","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"idsite","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The site ID the encoder is made with"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rec"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", without which Matomo records nothing","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"apiv"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":", the Tracking API’s version"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The visitor: the last 64 bits of the record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as 16 lowercase hexadecimal digits; of the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cdt"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in whole seconds since 1970, rounded down"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ca"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":": the request is an event, not a page view, should Matomo’s Events plugin be turned off","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_c"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The category the encoder is made with"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_a"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"lang","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s locale’s BCP 47 identifier, "},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when its context has a "},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"dimension<ID>","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each mapped property’s value, by the dimension’s ID, from lowest to highest"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent. Matomo counts a visitor per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its visitors are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions, each a new visitor of one visit. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own visitor, linked to nothing. A record a store recovers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token_auth"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cip"},{"type":"text","text":" or device"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier is sent, and nothing of the record’s context but its locale, nor its trace context."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property reaches Matomo only as the custom dimension ","type":"text"},{"code":"dimensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" maps it to, read through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads it: a string as it is, a number as JSON","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes it, a Boolean as ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and an array or object as its JSON. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out, and an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every other property is left out, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder logs a notice once, when it is made, for each event of the plan with properties no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dimension is mapped to (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions\/unmappedProperties(in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write, or that Matomo would refuse or store other than it is, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are sent: one whose event and version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Matomo would empty or cut short, one whose event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no whole seconds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64"},{"text":" or is more than 23 hours before or after the batch is encoded, one with a dimension’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value longer than Matomo keeps, and one whose request is over 1,000,000 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError"},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EncodedRequest\/deadline"},{"type":"text","text":" is 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" drops a request still being retried by then, every record of it, the younger"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ones included, and reports it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":", rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than send it to a Matomo that would answer 200 and store nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. Matomo answers 200 to a bulk request it reads, counting the tracking requests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it refuses as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid"},{"text":" in its answer without storing them; 400 to a body it can’t read, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" drops and reports with every record of the request; and 500 when its database","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" retries. A 200 that says Matomo tracked none of the request’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracking requests is rejected (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"},{"text":"), so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" drops and reports it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"too; one that refused only some isn’t, as its answer doesn’t say which. It doesn’t remove duplicates, so a record sent again is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted again. The bytes are the same for the same records, time and configuration on every run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and platform.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"MatomoEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"MatomoBatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MatomoBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder.swift#L82","fileName":"MatomoBatchEncoder.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MatomoBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:14MatomoEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Matomo’s bulk tracking API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to a Matomo installation’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/matomo.php"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/init(siteID:dimensions:category:plan:limit:now:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"title":"Instanc